---
// Lead in old paint and tap water (#222 life areas, a gap named in wave 9;
// sprint wave 11). Facts come from the records, each read on the WV
// Childhood Lead Poisoning Prevention Project, Monongalia County Health
// Department and EPA pages on 2026-11-02. Left off: the Morgantown Utility
// Board's lead service line inventory and water quality report (mub.org's
// lead pages were not found during its site rebuild; see #1574), and any blood lead level number (state pages
// give two different numbers).
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import OnThisPage from '../components/OnThisPage.astro';
import ResourceCard from '../components/ResourceCard.astro';
import { resource } from '../lib/content.mjs';
import { fixFormUrl } from '../lib/group-requests.mjs';
export const page = { door: "living-here", topic: "safety", label: "Lead in old paint and tap water", summary: "Blood lead tests for young children, a lead test at the health department, lead-safe work on homes built before 1978, renters' rights, and lowering lead in tap water" };
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Base title="Lead in paint and tap water in Morgantown and Mon County, WV" description="Lead help in Monongalia County, WV: blood lead tests for children at ages 1 and 2, finger stick lead tests at the Monongalia County Health Department, EPA's lead-safe rule for homes built before 1978, what renters can do, and ways to lower lead in tap water.">
  <h1>Lead in old paint and tap water</h1>
  <p class="lede">A blood test is the only way to know if someone has too much lead. West Virginia's rule says every child gets a lead test at age 1 and again at age 2. The health department gives a finger stick test to anyone 1 or older.</p>
  <OnThisPage items={[['#test', "Get a lead test"], ['#paint', "Old paint and repairs"], ['#rent', "If you rent"], ['#water', "Tap water"]]} />

  <h2 id="test">Get a lead test</h2>
  <ResourceCard r={resource('wv-child-blood-lead-test')} />
  <ResourceCard r={resource('monchd-lead-test')} showCost />

  <h2 id="paint">Old paint and repairs</h2>
  <ResourceCard r={resource('epa-lead-safe-contractor')} />

  <h2 id="rent">If you rent</h2>
  <ResourceCard r={resource('epa-lead-paint-renters-report')} />
  <p>More on renting: <a href={`${base}/renting/`}>Renting a home</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="water">Tap water</h2>
  <ResourceCard r={resource('epa-reduce-lead-in-tap-water')} />
  <p>Wondering whether the pipe to your home is lead? Ask your water utility. Not sure who that is? See <a href={`${base}/who-serves-me/`}>Who serves my address</a>.</p>

  <p class="meta">Sources checked November 2, 2026. Something out of date? <a href={fixFormUrl({ page: Astro.url.pathname })}>Tell us</a>.</p>
</Base>
